# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_conflict_anticipation.py" "CONFLICT ANTICIPATION GATE: PASS" "merge-conflict anticipation" "merge-conflict anticipation (main_impact_surface exposes merge_conflict_likely/conflict_points from the SAME content-free line ranges as finer-collision; overlap OR same-insertion-point [bounded gap] = likely, disjoint-with-gap = not flagged [no false conflict]; INDEPENDENT of the verdict so a softened run_gates.sh-class collision keeps its soft severity AND gains the conflict heads-up [the regression that bit us]; rendered honestly 'likely'/'expect' never 'will definitely'; no diff body stored/rendered)" "merge-conflict anticipation (a DIFFERENT axis from severity: overlapping/same-insertion-point line ranges → likely git conflict; disjoint-with-gap NOT flagged; a SOFTENED low-value collision still forewarns the conflict; honest 'likely' not 'will'; content-free)" 20
